netlink: configure hairpin and learning on bridge ports (upstream PR 16233)

What: RTM_SETLINK with ifi_family AF_BRIDGE and a nested IFLA_PROTINFO sets
the hairpin (IFLA_BRPORT_MODE) and learning (IFLA_BRPORT_LEARNING) options of
a bridge port, as net/core/rtnetlink.c:rtnl_bridge_setlink() and
net/bridge/br_netlink.c:br_setlink() do, and the bridge honors both: in
hairpin mode a frame may go back out of the port it came in on
(net/bridge/br_forward.c:should_deliver()), and without learning the port's
source addresses are not recorded (br_handle_frame_finish()). A new port
starts with learning on and hairpin off, as in Linux's br_add_if(), which is
what gVisor's bridge did. Other port options still fail with EOPNOTSUPP.

Why: the CNI bridge plugin sets hairpin mode on every container veth it adds
to a bridge and fails the attachment when that fails. Podman 4.9.3's CNI
backend, Ubuntu 24.04's default when netavark is not installed, failed every
container on a network of its own: "plugin type=bridge failed (add): failed
to setup hairpin mode for vethX: operation not supported".

Upstream: google/gvisor PR 16233 (top commit 5513a14b9b1a, open on
2026-11-17), applied to release-20261109.0's bridge. Upstream stacks it on PR
16230 (commit e1d29de2d, in master since 2026-11-12), which ALE leaves out:
besides keeping frames for the bridge's own addresses out of its ports, it
makes IPv4, IPv6 and ARP drop frames addressed to another host on every
interface, as Linux does, and with it a container that Docker restarts in a
sandbox, which comes back with another MAC address, was unreachable through
its published port for about 30 s, until the sandbox's neighbor entry for it
expired: 8 of the 9 Docker installs of the nested checks failed their stop and
start. Docker announces the new address with a gratuitous ARP, which needs a
packet socket that runsc-nested does not give ("Failed to prepare unsolicited
ARP ... create socket: operation not permitted"). So the bridge forwards as
in release-20261109.0, flags aside, and the PR's check that a frame for the
bridge's or a port's own address never goes back out, which needs PR 16230,
is left out of its test; such a frame is still flooded, as before. Drop this
patch once the gVisor release ALE builds from has PR 16233, and check then
that Docker's stop and start still pass with PR 16230.

Verified:
- The PR's syscall tests BridgePortTest.SetHairpinAndLearning,
  .SetUnknownInterface and .SetEmptyAttribute pass on runsc with this patch,
  under the runtime arguments of runsc and of runsc-nested, and fail on ALE's
  0.1.2; the whole socket_netlink_route_test passes (126 tests with patches
  0012 to 0014). The PR's unit tests in //pkg/tcpip/stack:bridge_test
  (TestBridgePortHairpin, TestBridgePortLearning, TestBridgePortFlagsAPI),
  //pkg/sentry/socket/netlink/route:route_test and
  //pkg/sentry/socket/netstack:netstack_test pass, as do stack_test and
  stack_x_test.
- Podman 4.9.3's CNI backend in an Ubuntu 24.04 sandbox under runsc-nested
  attached its containers to its bridge; with the patches up to 0018 it passed
  the nested checks, and Docker's stop and start passed as with 0.1.2
  (README.md).

